    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** providing the clear offensive anchor; his 80.65 efficiency score is driven by an elite .469 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Rocker, whose 4.31 xERA allows for significant damage. We are also leaning heavily into the speed-weighted upside of **Christian Yelich** (74.33) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (69.78). Despite the rain risks in their respective contests, both players are start-essential, as they face vulnerable pitchers with high \"Slow SP Delivery\" metrics\u2014a critical factor for our stolen base-starved 5x5 Roto strategy. **Yelich** specifically benefits from a 100% stolen base opportunity window against Chandler, making him one of our most potent weapons today despite the 31% precipitation forecast.\n\nDecisions on the fringes remain tight, particularly with **Luke Raley**, who sits on our bench with a 44.02 score. **Raley** was the closest to cracking the lineup, but he was ultimately squeezed out by the superior platoon and order stability of **Chase Meidroth** and **Junior Caminero**. While **Caminero** faces a daunting test against Logan Gilbert (3.35 xERA), his consistent middle-order role in a high-leverage slot outweighs the marginal efficiency gains offered by **Raley**. Meanwhile, the optimizer continues to signal caution regarding **Dillon Dingler** (46.92) and **Casey Schmitt** (45.28); both are hovering near our bench floor due to difficult opposing arms, but remain active to preserve our aggregate position production. Managers should keep a close eye on the weather; the 45% rain risk for **Caleb Durbin** could force a late-scramble if the game at Peralta\u2019s stadium is suspended, potentially requiring a pivot to our bench depth.",
